# integratevolume

- Label: Integrate Volume
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 6
- Parameters: 23 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/integratevolume.html
- Summary (EN): Integrates a VDB along each camera view ray, computing the line integral, transmittance, minimum or maximum per pixel. It shows how much of a volume lies under each pixel, for example heat distortion driven by a temperature VDB.
- Résumé (FR) : Intègre un VDB le long des rayons de la caméra pour obtenir l'intégrale, la transmittance, le minimum ou le maximum par pixel.

- Inputs meaning: ["camera_ref: optional camera defining view rays and the imaging plane", "density: the Float or Vector VDB to integrate", "vieworigin: per-pixel ray origins, used instead of camera_ref", "viewdir: per-pixel ray directions, used instead of camera_ref", "mindepth: raymarch minimum boundary", "maxdepth: raymarch maximum boundary"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Operation", "meaning": "Integral, Transmittance, Minimum or Maximum"}, {"name": "Depth Conversion", "meaning": "Distance, Depth or Height; sets how mindepth and maxdepth are read"}, {"name": "Density Min/Max, Ramp Mode, Density Ramp, Density Scale", "meaning": "remap and shape density before integration"}, {"name": "Integration Step Size", "meaning": "length of each ray slice"}, {"name": "Jitter Scales", "meaning": "reduce banding in sample and slice placement"}, {"name": "Max Step Count", "meaning": "safety limit, default 4096"}, {"name": "Transmittance Cutoff", "meaning": "early termination; -1 disables it"}]

- Caveats: ["Transmittance Cutoff can cause false zero transmittance in very dense volumes through rounding error; use -1 for fields that are not optical densities.", "Minimum and Maximum return infinity or -infinity when no ray hits."]

